<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23273" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαίω</span></b>  (B), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>divide</i>:—
				Act.
			 is not found in this sense (for aor.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔδαισα</span>
			
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαίνυμι</span>
			)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, δαΐζω</span> being used:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαίεται ἦτορ</span> my heart
				<i>is torn, distracted,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				1.48
			</span></i>: 
				Ep.
			
			3pl.
			pf., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αἰθίοπας, τοὶ διχθὰ
				δεδαίαται</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				23
			</span></i>: —more freq. in 
				Med.
			, <i>distribute,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρέα δαίετο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					15.140
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρέα πολλὰ δαιόμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					17.332
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πήματα . . δαίονται βροτοῖς ἀθάνατοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					3.81
				</span></i>
			; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δατέομαι.</span>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			aor.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔδαισα,</span>
			<i>feast,</i> from <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
			</span></i> downwards, though formed from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαίω,</span> belongs in sense to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαίνυμι</span> (q. v.):—
				Med.
			, <i>feast on,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ἀμβροσίην] δαίονται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Matro
					<u>Conv.</u>
					72
				</span></i>
			. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαι-</span> also in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαίς, δαίνυμι,</span> etc.: prob. akin to
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δα-</span> in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δατέομαι.</span>)</div>
